 "notes": "Part B (subsidiary language by mother tongue); subsidiary = big heading, mother_tongue = sub-heading. Block 1 opens with NAIPALI (serial 25, from Part I) continued from leaf 219: its BENGAL 'All mother tongues' total and earlier sub-headings are on leaf 219, so no total check here. RONG (28; 11) continues from block 1 into block 2 (Limbu, Murmi, Naipali, Khambu, English); its 'All mother tongues' total is checked against all its sub-entries. Sub-headings whose only row is a single district are printed in bold with no BENGAL row; recorded as the district row. Records with footnote_mark '*' (Bara/Bengali, Garo/Assamese, Khasi/English) carry the page footnote. LUSHEI (35) figures are for Chittagong Hill Tracts only, no BENGAL row. Checks: every BENGAL row equals the sum of its district rows; each 'All mother tongues' total equals the sum of its sub-entries (Rai, Rong, Assamese, Kherwari, Kurukh; Newari and Lushei district rows also agree)."
